@page "/docs/components/input-date"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.InputDate
<PageTitle>Input Date - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Input Date</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="input-date" />
        </div>
        <p>An inline field bound to a <code>DateOnly</code>, where you type or arrow-step the day, month and year in place. <code>Format</code> sets the order of those segments and the separators between them, and an optional trailing button opens a <a href="/docs/components/calendar">Calendar</a> popup. Pair it with <a href="/docs/components/input-time">Input Time</a> when you need both a date and a time.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(InputDateUsageExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, bind a nullable `DateOnly` to `Value`. Type digits and focus moves to the next segment on its own, or step a segment with the arrow keys." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Basic" Description="The default `yyyy-MM-dd` layout with a leading calendar icon."
          Example="typeof(InputDateBasicExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Format" Description="`Format` reorders the segments and sets the separators. It accepts any mix of `d`, `M` and `y` runs with literal text between them."
          Example="typeof(InputDateFormatExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With calendar popup" Description="`ShowCalendar` adds a trailing button that opens the calendar. Picking a day fills the segments and closes the popup, and `Min`, `Max` and `Culture` are passed through to the calendar."
          Example="typeof(InputDateCalendarExample)" />

    <Demo Title="No icon" Description="Set `ShowIcon` to `false` to drop the leading icon, or pass `Icon` to use your own."
          Example="typeof(InputDateNoIconExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Programmatic focus" Description="Keep a reference to the component and call `FocusAsync` to move focus yourself. Here a shortcut sets the date and focuses the first segment, and `Select` highlights it so the value can be typed over right away."
          Example="typeof(InputDateFocusMethodExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Auto focus" Description="`AutoFocus` focuses the first segment as soon as the field appears. Each segment selects its contents on focus, so typing replaces the value. `BzInputTime` has the same parameter."
          Example="typeof(InputDateAutoFocusExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Description="`Disabled` dims the field and blocks editing."
          Example="typeof(InputDateDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Date and time" Description="Place it next to Input Time for a compact date and time row. Each field binds its own value."
          Example="typeof(InputDateDateTimeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Classes passed through `Class` style the field, such as its width, radius and a brand focus ring. The `Icon` slot swaps the leading icon."
          Example="typeof(InputDateCustomExample)" />
</div>

